 "title": "Build Micrograd from Scratch",
 "blurb": "Grow a tiny scalar autograd engine one piece at a time: measure slopes numerically, wrap numbers in Value nodes that remember their history, write backward rules and a topological backward pass, then stack neurons into an MLP and train it with your own gradients.",
 "prereq": "Comfortable Python (classes, closures, operator overloading) and derivatives at school level; the chain rule is used constantly, so a quick refresher on it helps.",
 "next": "Move from scalars to arrays: rewrite the engine on NumPy tensors with matrix-valued backward rules, or compare it with how PyTorch's autograd records and replays the same graph.",
